<===> README.md
Self assignments like `$l: list.append($l, ...)` may modify the list in
place. The variable must still be found if evaluating the arguments grows the
variable stack (e.g. via deep recursion), which reallocates it.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> append_with_deep_calls/input.scss
@use "sass:list";
@use "sass:map";
@function deep($n) { @if $n <= 0 { @return 0; } $a: 1; $b: 2; $c: 3; @return deep($n - 1) + 1; }
$l: ();
$m: ();
@for $i from 1 through 50 { $l: list.append($l, deep(300)); $m: map.merge($m, ($i: deep(300))); }
a { b: list.length($l); c: list.nth($l, 50); d: map.get($m, 50); e: list.length(map.keys($m)); }
<===> append_with_deep_calls/output.css
a {
  b: 50;
  c: 300;
  d: 300;
  e: 50;
}
